               same, because the one thing a person could do about it is
               obvious and worth saying. */
            'invalid_intake_item_name',
            /* Two items of one team naming different editors. The dialog sends
               a single choice, so this is a malformed submission rather than a
               race the person can resolve by retrying. */
            'intake_assignee_override_conflict',
            /* The card only offers the fill button for a component it can see
               is missing, beside a sibling it can see. Reaching either of these
               means a request this UI did not build. */
            'invalid_component_fill_payload', 'invalid_component_fill_route',
            'invalid_intake_video_number', 'invalid_production_create_payload',
            'invalid_production_create_scope', 'unsupported_create_field',
            'label_selection_invalid',
            /* The two parent-lookup refusals. `comment_parent_ambiguous` sat in
