    /* Codes whose advice is more specific than their class. The first four are
       the messages this notification already carried; they stay word for word,
       and only gain the code suffix every other message now carries. */
    const WRITE_UI_FAILURE_CODE_TEXT = {
        /* THE THREE REFUSALS THAT STOP BEING TRANSIENT ON 2026-09-15.
           WRITE_UI_FAILURE_CODE_CLASS files all three under `wait` -- correct
           today, because each one means a dependency was unreachable and
           nothing was committed, and the dependency usually comes back. It
           stops being correct the day the Linear account lapses: the gateway
           raises the identical code, and `wait` then advises an SMM to keep
           trying something that can never succeed again. That is the exact
           shape of the 2026-08-26 incident, where "safe to retry" cost a
           videographer eleven identical submissions.
           These entries do not reclassify anything -- this object exists for
           "codes whose advice is more specific than their class" -- they add
           the two sentences the class cannot carry: it is NOT this client's
           setup, and if it does not clear on its own, no amount of retrying
           will clear it. See OPEN_REPAIRS 170. */
        project_mapping_validation_unavailable: {
            title: 'Post not created',
            text: 'The linked task system could not be reached, so this post was not filed. Nothing was created. This is not a problem with this client\u2019s setup and no setting will fix it \u2014 if it does not clear on its own within a few minutes, report it rather than trying again.'
        },
        batch_parent_validation_unavailable: {
