        public_intake_rate_unavailable: {
            title: 'Submission not sent',
            text: 'We could not finish checking this submission, so nothing was sent. What you typed is still here — please try again in a moment.'
        },
        /* "Reload before trying again" was false, and the comment fifteen lines
           above _writeUiClassifyTargetless already said so: makePayload throws
           this "forever after", from the row own state. Nothing here reads a
           cache, and no client-side path backfills a deliverable id from a url
           -- the adopter runs the other way -- so a reload re-reads the same
           server row and refuses identically. Measured live 2026-08-31, cards
           not archived: 111 carry a Linear video link with no deliverable id and
           149 the graphics equivalent, and 36 of the 111 are still in flight.
           The pill is not even locked for them: _calCompLinked is true when
           EITHER the url or the id is present.

           The message now says what is wrong and stops prescribing. It
           deliberately does NOT name a remedy: post-flip there is no in-app way
           to give a legacy card a native work item -- creation is closed, the
           link paste is sealed, and Import from Linear only makes more of them
           -- so the honest remedy is an escalation, and which one is the
           owner call to make (OPEN_REPAIRS 87.14). Saying less is better than
           something the reader cannot act on.

           Do NOT "fix" this by adding native_link_required to the cache-eviction
           list in _writeUiReportFailure. That list exists to MAKE reload advice
           true for entity_not_found and batch_not_found; here the server row is
           the problem, so eviction would force a full refetch per client across
           260 cards and still refuse. */
        native_link_required: {
            title: 'Write not saved',
            text: 'This card is linked to a Linear issue but has no SyncView work item behind it, so its status cannot be changed here. Reloading will not change that — the card has to be linked to one first.'
        },
        authority_unavailable: {
            title: 'Write paused safely',
            text: 'Team authority could not be verified. Reload and try again; no Linear write was attempted.'
