           identically, forever. The round-3 tester hit this as Create Post
           being completely broken with an error that invited them to keep
           trying (PR 1186). Naming browser storage is what makes it
           actionable; the per-client cache that filled it is now capped, so
           this should become rare rather than routine. */
        native_intake_storage_unavailable: {
            title: 'Post not created',
            text: 'This browser has run out of storage, so the new post could not be staged — and retrying will fail the same way until space is freed. Close other tabs of this site, or clear this site’s browser storage, then create it again. Nothing was saved, so nothing is half-made.'
