           around that: copy first, because the refusal itself is deterministic
           and nothing is lost by taking a moment.

           Neither says "reload". `comment_parent_ambiguous` sat in the reload
           class from the day it was written, so the person hitting it was told
           to reload a page whose stale copy was never the problem -- the parent
           row is resolved from stored rows on the server, identically on every
           attempt -- and the reload it asked for is what would have thrown the
           text away. That is OPEN_REPAIRS 13 in a different costume, and the
           `reload` class text is the one that DOES belong to a stale tab.

