           two-transport split made visible: a root whose card fails the F42
           crosswalk was written to the legacy card store with no canonical row
           behind it, and a reply routed to the gateway asks for a parent that
           was never sent there. The add lane now routes an unlinked card
           legacy, which is what stops it happening (see _calAppendComment), so
           this should be a stale tab loaded before that shipped -- but the
           remedy named here works either way, and needs no explaining. */
        comment_parent_not_found: {
            title: 'Reply not saved',
            text: 'The note you replied to is not in the production thread this reply was sent to, so nothing was saved. Copy your text out of the note box first — a reply draft lives only in this tab. Sending it again will be refused the same way; post it as a new note on the card instead, and send this code to the owner so the thread can be joined back up.'
        },
        comment_parent_ambiguous: {
            title: 'Reply not saved',
            text: 'Two production notes answer to the identifier this reply names, so the thread it belongs to cannot be told apart and nothing was saved. Copy your text out of the note box first — a reply draft lives only in this tab. Sending it again will not change the answer; post it as a new note on the card instead, and send this code and the card to the owner, who has to separate the two notes.'
        },
